// Wi-Fi onboarding QR, two sizes, generated from PhotoFrameApp.cpp's AP_SSID /
// AP_PASSWORD so they cannot drift from what the board broadcasts:
//   WIFI:T:WPA;S:Jimny_Dash_Sync;P:password123;;
//
// STORED AS INDEXED_1BIT, NOT RGB565A8. A QR is two colours; RGB565A8 spends
// three bytes per pixel on it. As RGB565A8 these two assets were 349KB and
// overflowed the 3.7MB app partition, leaving the board with no bootable image
// — note that arduino-cli reports flash usage against the 16MB CHIP, not against
// the partition, so it looked like 23% right up until it would not boot. As
// 1-bit they are ~14KB together.
//
// THREE THINGS ARE LOAD-BEARING, each learned by breaking it:
//
// 1. The 4-module white quiet zone is baked in. The original asset had the
//    finder pattern starting at pixel 0 and no camera would lock on — while
//    still looking like a fine QR to a human eye.
// 2. Module size. The original was 6.86px and scanned; a 4px regeneration did
//    not. The large variant is 7px, deliberately above the size known to work.
// 3. Error correction L, not M. A screen has no dirt to correct for, so M's
//    redundancy cost four modules of width for nothing.
//
// DRAW AT NATIVE SIZE — this was once drawn at zoom 215, a 0.84x downscale, and
// resampling a bitmap QR by a non-integer factor smears module edges until a
// camera cannot resolve them. To resize, regenerate; do not scale.

// wifi_qrcode: 222x222 — 29 modules at 6px plus a 4-module quiet zone.
